                                "sense_id": "5493f507-8e8f-3251-8d7b-c27cd16d4b0e",
                                "text": "The house boats of the Mohannas are called “Doondees“. One family may live in the same small boat for as long as half a century. These “Doondees“ range in size between 6 m long and 2 m wide up to a length of 14 m and a width of 4 m in the middle of the boat. The boat is basically steered by a gibstaff."
                            }
